-- Reference migration for the relational OAuth state store
-- (`TomSqlOAuthStateStore`).
--
-- Creates the `tom_oauth_state` table: one row per authorization that has been
-- begun and not yet completed. This file is the canonical DDL and is kept in
-- sync with `oauthStateTableDdl()` in
-- `lib/src/tomserver/authentication/oauth_state_sql.dart`;
-- `test/framework_schema_test.dart` fails if the two drift apart.
--
-- Apply this only where the store is configured `type: sql`. A single-node
-- deployment keeps the in-process store and needs no table. The reason a
-- cluster does need one is that the two halves of an authorization-code flow
-- are two separate HTTP requests, and the second is a redirect the *provider*
-- issues — it lands on whichever node the load balancer picks, which on a
-- cluster is a coin flip. A pending authorization held in one process is
-- therefore invisible to the node that has to complete it.
--
-- Several columns are not obvious:
--
--  * `state` is the primary key and *is* the record's identity — the opaque
--    handle the provider echoes back. There is deliberately no surrogate key:
--    a second row for the same handle would make "which pending flow does this
--    callback complete" depend on row order, which is the one question the
--    table exists to answer unambiguously.
--  * `expires_at` is stored rather than derived from `created_at` plus the
--    store's time-to-live. The TTL is a property of the *node* that happened to
--    begin the flow, and in a cluster two nodes can be configured differently
--    or rolled out at different times; writing the deadline makes expiry a
--    property of the record, so a flow begun under a ten-minute TTL is not
--    silently extended by a peer configured for thirty. It also lets the
--    completion statement carry expiry as an ordinary `WHERE` predicate rather
--    than having to know a TTL at all.
--  * `created_at` is kept anyway, because it is what an operator reads when
--    asking how long a flow sat unfinished — a question `expires_at` alone
--    cannot answer once the TTL has been changed.
--  * `pkce_verifier` is the flow's secret and is nullable, because a provider
--    may be configured without PKCE. It is stored as written rather than under
--    column encryption; see the library dartdoc of
--    `sql_oauth_state_store.dart` for why, and encrypt the tablespace if your
--    deployment is regulated.
--  * `nonce` is what the flow's next leg must echo: the OpenID Connect nonce,
--    or a SAML `AuthnRequest` id and then the digest of the handoff code. It
--    holds `''` when the flow sent none.
--  * `asserted_identity` holds a verified SAML identity, as JSON, between the
--    identity provider's form post and the application's completion. `TEXT`
--    because a SAML assertion's attributes have no fixed size, and `NULL` on
--    every record that is not waiting to be completed.
--  * the login-context columns (`client` … `client_timezone`) exist because the
--    callback is a bare browser navigation carrying none of it. They are
--    `NOT NULL` and hold `''` for "not supplied", matching the Dart record
--    whose fields default to the empty string — a nullable column would
--    introduce a second spelling of absence that every read would collapse.
--  * `tenant` is the tenant the flow began in, `''` for none. Every read and
--    the completion name the tenant in context, so a callback that reaches
--    another tenant finds no record and cannot spend it.
--  * `ix_tom_oauth_state_expiry` is the index the sweep rides. Without it,
--    pruning is a full scan of a table whose whole point is to be swept often.
--
-- Instants are `DATETIME(6)` and are always written in UTC.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tom_oauth_state (
  state VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  provider_id VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  pkce_verifier VARCHAR(191) NULL,
  pkce_challenge VARCHAR(191) NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMP(6) NOT NULL,
  expires_at TIMESTAMP(6) NOT NULL,
  client VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  application VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  process VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  organization VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  client_language VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
  client_country VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
  client_timezone VARCHAR(64) NOT NULL,
  nonce VARCHAR(191) NOT NULL,
  asserted_identity TEXT NULL,
  tenant VARCHAR(32) NOT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (state)
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_tom_oauth_state_expiry ON tom_oauth_state (expires_at);
